"MC-410-INFO  How to Request a Disability Accommodation for Court (https://courts.ca.gov/sites/default/files/courts/default/2024-11/mc410info.pdf)\nciteturn1709search12 [wordlim: 200] Published: 5.7 years ago; Crawled: 5.7 years ago; MC-410-INFO — How to Request a Disability Accommodation for Court\nMC-410-INFO — How to Request a Disability Accommodation for Court\n\nThe court will respond to your request by telling you in person, calling you on the phone, or mailing or emailing you a response.\n\nPage 2 of form MC-410 is where the court responds to your request.\n\n<visual_element id=\"e1\">\nWarning box with exclamation icon. Text: “Important! If your case is delayed or dismissed after you make your request, please contact the court at the phone number or email address provided.”\n</visual_element>\n\n- The court will check one of two boxes. Either:\n\n  Your Request is **GRANTED**\n\n  -OR-\n\n  Your Request is **DENIED IN WHOLE OR IN PART**\n\n  If your request is denied in whole or in part, the court will tell you **why** it is being denied. If the court offers you a different accommodation, it will tell you **what accommodation** will be provided.\n\n- If the court will provide an accommodation, it will tell you **when** the accommodation will be provided: either the dates and times you requested, indefinitely, or for different dates and times.\n\n- If the court provides additional information about the decision, it will check that box and attach the information to the form.\n\n- Underneath the court's signature line, the court enters a date telling you **when** the court responded to the request. The court may respond by telling you in person, calling you on the phone, or by mailing or emailing you a response.\n\n- At the bottom of the page, there is a link to information about how to ask for a review or the court's decision.\n\nNeed More Help?\n\n- See\n- Visit your court's website to find the ADA Coordinator.\n  - For help finding your court:\n\nNew January 1, 2021  \nHow to Request a Disability Accommodation for Court  \nMC-410-INFO, Page 3 of 3 →--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nHow to Request a Disability Accommodation for Court | California Courts | Self Help Guide (https://www.selfhelp.courts.ca.gov/jcc-form/MC-410-INFO)\nciteturn1709search0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; # How to Request a Disability Accommodation for Court (MC-410-INFO)\n\n# How to Request a Disability Accommodation for Court (MC-410-INFO)\n\nExplains how to fill out a disability accommodation request (form MC-410).\n\nGet form MC-410-INFO\n\n  * 汉语Get form MC-410-INFO in Chinese Simplified (Chinese Simplified)\n  * 한국어Get form MC-410-INFO in Korean (Korean)\n  * españolGet form MC-410-INFO in Spanish (Spanish)\n  * Tiếng ViệtGet form MC-410-INFO in Vietnamese (Vietnamese)\n\nEffective: January 1, 2021--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nMC-410-INFO (https://www.courts.ca.gov/documents/mc410info.pdf)\nciteturn1709search13 [wordlim: 200] Published: 2.1 years ago; MC-410-INFO ... Page 1 of form MC-410 asks for the information the court needs to understand and ... www.courts.ca.gov\nMC-410-INFO\nHow to Request a Disability Accommodation for Court\nThis information sheet is for form                                                                         .\nMC-410 (Disability Accommodation Request)\nThe purpose of this information sheet is to help you:\nl Ask the court for an accommodation on page 1 of form MC-410.\nl Understand the court's response on page 2.\nIf you have a disability or limitation and need an accommodation while you are at \ncourt, one way to ask for an accommodation is to fill out form MC-410 and give it to \nthe ADA Coordinator or designated person (this could be a court clerk, a jury \ncommissioner, or another person). Other ways to ask for an accommodation are to \ncall the court or go in person to ask the ADA Coordinator or designated person.\nPlease note: If you are submitting papers to the court electronically, through \nelectronic filing, you must not include form MC-410 with your filing. Form MC-410 is \na confidential form that is not part of the case file. The form must be given to the \nADA Coordinator or designated person in your court.\nMake this request at least 5 days (when the court is open) before you \nneed the accommodation. \nIf this is not possible, you can still make a request.\nPage 1 of form MC-410 asks for the information the court needs to understand and \nmake a decision about your request.\nCourt name and Address:\nWrite the name and address of your court. If you \ndo not know the court address, ask the ADA \nCoordinator or court staff for help.\nCase Number (if you know it):\nIf you have a case number, write it here.\nCase Name/Type (if you know it):\nIf you know the name of your case, write it here. \n \nExample: Guardianship of Jane Doe.\nMC-410-INFO, Page 1 of 3\nwww.courts.ca.gov\nJudicial Council of California,  \n \nNew January 1, 2021, Optional Form \nCal. Rules of Court, rule 1.100\n How to Request a Disability \nAccommodation for Court--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nMC-410-INFO  How to Request a Disability Accommodation for Court (https://courts.ca.gov/system/files/file/rules-20200820-materials.pdf)\nciteturn1709search14 [wordlim: 200] Published: 6.1 years ago; MC-410-INFO  How to Request a Disability Accommodation for Court\nMC-410-INFO  How to Request a Disability Accommodation for Court\n\nThis information sheet is for form MC-410 (Disability Accommodation Request).\n\nThe purpose of this information sheet is to help you:\n- Ask the court for an accommodation on page 1 of form MC-410.\n- Understand the court’s response on page 2.\n\nIf you have a disability or limitation and need an accommodation while you are at court, one way to ask for an accommodation is to fill out form MC-410 and give it to the ADA Coordinator or designated person (this could be a court clerk, a jury commissioner, or another person). Other ways to ask for an accommodation are to call the court or go in person to ask the ADA Coordinator or designated person.\n\nPlease note: If you are submitting papers to the court electronically, through electronic filing, you must not include form MC-410 with your filing. Form MC-410 is a confidential form that is not part of the case file. The form must be given to the ADA Coordinator or designated person in your court.\n\nMake this request at least 5 days (when the court is open) before you need the accommodation. If this is not possible, you can still make a request.\n\nPage 1 of form MC-410 asks for the information the court needs to understand and make a decision about your request.\n\nCourt Name and Address:\nWrite the name and address of your court. If you do not know the court address, ask the ADA Coordinator or court staff for help.\n\nCase Number (if you know it):\nIf you have a case number, write it here.\n\nCase Name/Type (if you know it):\nIf you know the name of your case, write it here.\nExample: Guardianship of Jane Doe\n\n<visual_element id=\"e1\">\nCalendar icon with the number 5, indicating “at least 5 days.”\n</visual_element>\n\n<visual_element id=\"e2\">\nSample form fields shown on the right side: “Court Name and Address,” “Case Number (if you know it),” and “Case Name/Type (if you know it)” with blank entry boxes.\n</visual_element>--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nHow to Request a Disability Accommodation for Court | California Courts | Self Help Guide (https://selfhelp.courts.ca.gov/jcc-form/MC-410-INFO)\nciteturn1709search1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; # How to Request a Disability Accommodation for Court (MC-410-INFO)\n\n# How to Request a Disability Accommodation for Court (MC-410-INFO)\n\nExplains how to fill out a disability accommodation request (form MC-410).\n\nGet form MC-410-INFO\n\nEffective: January 1, 2021--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nAppeals forms | California Courts | Self Help Guide (https://selfhelp.courts.ca.gov/appeals/forms)\nciteturn1709search2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; How to Request a Disability Accommodation for Court  | MC-410-INFO\nInformation Sheet for Proof of Service (Court of Appeal)  | APP-009 INFO\nRespondent’s Notice Designating Record on Appeal  | APP-010\nStipulation for Extension of Time to File Brief  | APP-012\nMemorandum of Costs on Appeal  | APP-013\nAppellant's Proposed Settled Statement  | APP-014\nOther Party and Nonparty Witness Testimony and Other Evidence Attachment  | APP-014A\nInformation Sheet for Proposed Settled Statement  | APP-014-INFO\nInformation Sheet on Waiver of Appellate Court Fees  | APP-015/FW-015-INFO\nOrder on Court Fee Waiver  | APP-016/FW-016\nResponse to Appellant’s Proposed Settled Statement (Unlimited Civil Case)  | APP-020\nOrder on Appellant’s Proposed Settled Statement (Unlimited Civil Case)  | APP-022\nAppellant’s Motion to Use a Settled Statement  | APP-025\nAttached Declaration  | APP-031A\nRequest to Waive Court Fees  | FW-001\nInformation Sheet on Waiver of Superior Court Fees and Costs  | FW-001-INFO\nRequest for Accommodations by Persons with Disabilities and Response  | MC-410\nHow to Request a Disability Accommodation for Court  | MC-410-INFO\nRequest and Order to File New Litigation by Vexatious Litigant  | VL-110--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nHow to ask for a disability accommodation | California Courts | Self Help Guide (https://www.selfhelp.courts.ca.gov/how-ask-disability-accommodation)\nciteturn1709search3 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 3 weeks ago;     * If you file court documents online, called e-filing, do not include it with your other public filings. ... 📘 Get more detailed instructions in How to Request a Disability Accommodation for Court (form MC-410-INFO) ↗️.\nYou can use Find my court ↗️ to go to the court's website and look under \"ADA\" for information about the local process.\n\n## How to ask for a disability accommodation\n\n↗️ All links below open in a new tab so you don’t lose your place.\n\n  * ### Fill out form\n\n    1. Fill out page 1 of Disability Accommodation Request (form MC-410) ↗️\n       * It asks for information the court needs to understand your request \n       * Do not fill out page 2\n    2. Sign at the bottom of page 1\n    3. The court will write its decision on page 2\n\n📘 Get more detailed instructions in How to Request a Disability Accommodation for Court (form MC-410-INFO) ↗️.\n\nThis information sheet is also available in:\n\n    * Español ↗️ (Spanish)\n    * 汉语 ↗️ (Chinese Simplified)\n    * 한국어 ↗️ (Korean)\n    * Tiếng Việt ↗️ (Vietnamese)\n\n  * ### Turn in the form\n\nTurn in the form to the court's ADA coordinator or other designated person.\n\n    * Contact the court ↗️ to find out how to turn in your request.\n    * You can usually submit your request in person, by mail, email, or fax.\n\n  * ### Get the court's response\n\n    * The court will respond to your request either in person, by pone, by mail or by email.\n      * The decision will be on page 2 of the request.\n    * If your request was not granted, the court's response will explain why.\n\nYou can find information about how to ask for a review of a denial in California Rule of Court 1.100(g) ↗️. (This law is written for lawyers and may be hard to understand.)--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n| California Courts | Self Help Guide (https://selfhelp.courts.ca.gov/find-forms/all-by-category)\nciteturn1709search4 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 5 days ago;   * APP-015-INFO * Information Sheet on Waiver of Appellate Court Fees—Supreme Court, Court of Appeal, Appellate Division Effective: March 1, 2026 汉语 한국어 español Tiếng Việt ...   * MC-410-INFO How to Request a 